{"title":"Conference Report and Intelligence Briefing: PCE/PCAH2025","link":"https://iafor.org/conference-report-and-intelligence-briefing-pce-pcah2025/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=conference-report-and-intelligence-briefing-pce-pcah2025","date":1758772839000,"content":"<img width=\"150\" height=\"150\" src=\"https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/PCE2025-Group-1500-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"PCE/PCAH2025 Conference Report\" srcset=\"https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/PCE2025-Group-1500-150x150.jpg 150w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/PCE2025-Group-1500-600x600.jpg 600w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/PCE2025-Group-1500-100x100.jpg 100w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/PCE2025-Group-1500-50x50.jpg 50w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/PCE2025-Group-1500-300x300.jpg 300w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/PCE2025-Group-1500-32x32.jpg 32w\" />PCE/PCAH2025 invited participants to engage with how we can rethink education and culture in a polarised world increasingly focused on defence, security, and the commercial value of ‘softpower’. The conference, hosted at the Sorbonne University International Conference Center, welcomed some 500 participants from 80 countries and over 400 institutions worldwide. \n<p><a href=\"https://iafor.org/conference-report-and-intelligence-briefing-pce-pcah2025/\">Source</a></p>","author":"IAFOR","siteTitle":"The International Academic Forum (IAFOR)","siteHash":"db6175d8277e1d8dd86d5cc607b1dd9335cce255aa7e00b46d0931f23a0d47f6","entryHash":"e981a051ac140899cf07faf8abfca46c401ef8c5ca0f3683144fbde83ab6c339","category":"Interdisciplinary"}